            <ArticleTitle>Creatinol O-phosphate therapy in patients with inadequate coronary circulation. Double-blind clinical trial.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1483-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>N-Methyl-N-(beta-hydroxyethyl) guanidine O-phosphate (creatinol O-phosphate, COP) was checked on patients suffering from inadequate coronary circulation (12 patients had a recent myocardial infarction and 13 were suffering from angina pectoris) versus a reference substance (solvent of COP) in a double blind study. COP improved rhythm disturbances, chest pains and symptoms of contractility failure to a statistically significant degree.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
